{
  "_doc": "Characters inherit a species and fix body colour (a name from colors below; it must match the skin in the character's drawn face), outfit (top: bare|full, bottom: briefs|dhoti) and cloth colour (a name from colors below, optionally with a pattern for rakshasas: red-check, red-diamond, red-stripe). Ids ending in a number (monkey1, raxas_m1) are generic types for unnamed figures. Defining features (necklaces, crowns, buns...) come later. scale (optional, default 1): body scale, torso and legs only (head, neck and arms keep their size); e.g. 0.8 for a small generic monkey. sideOnly (optional): the character is only ever drawn in side view — its face file has a side drawing only (the front layer is ignored), there is no head-turn data, and a panel asking for the front view gets the side view.",
